<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10359" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπίπτω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>collide,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				915b18
			</span></i>; <i>fall upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς σπείραις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					3.19.5
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>resist,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπῖπτον</span>”
				<i>resisting body,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					961b3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Act.Ap.</u>
					7.51
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδὲν ἀντιπεσόντα</span> without
				<i>demur</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>UPZ</u>
				36.21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς φράσεως οὐκ -ούσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Adv.</u>
					123.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ μηδὲν -πίπτει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1473.20
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aët.
				16.73
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιπῖπτον</span> an
				<i>objection,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Phlp.
				<u>in Mete.</u>
				58.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τοῦ ἀντιπίπτοντος
			λύσις</span> Aps.<i><span class="en">
				p.238H.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of circumstances, <i>to
				be adverse,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					16.2.1
				</span></i>
			, etc.: abs., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς τύχης
			-ούσης</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				28.2
			</span></i>; of contrary winds, <i><span class="en">
				4.44.9
			</span></i>; <i>tell against, conflict with</i> (fact or theory),
				<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Sign.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to fall in a contrary direction,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ σκιαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.1.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
